","lines":["Respiratory rate of 28 breaths per minute, heart rate is 110 beats per minute, blood pressure is 135/85 mmHg, and temperature is 37.2\u00b0C (99\u00b0F)"]},{"sid":25078,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, the patient is tachypneic with constricted pupils, diffuse muscle fasciculations, and wheezing on auscultation of the chest.","His skin is moist and there is a garlic-like odor."]},{"sid":25079,"type":"labs","lines":["Arterial blood gas shows a PaO2 of 60 mmHg, PaCO2 of 50 mmHg, and pH of 7.30."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":9061,"date":"2021-01-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. Marcus Johnson","cc":"suddenly collapsing","order":1,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4396],"sections":[{"sid":25080,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Suddenly collapsing"]},{"sid":25081,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns to the emergency department approximately one year following a prior ICU admission for similar symptoms including difficulty breathing, excessive salivation, and abdominal cramping.","He is brought by his brother after suddenly collapsing while working on a rural farm.","Earlier in the day, he had been spraying the crops with a chemical pesticide without wearing protective equipment.","According to his brother, the patient began complaining of dizziness, nausea, and difficulty seeing clearly.","Within minutes, he developed excessive sweating, abdominal cramps, and vomiting.","Shortly thereafter, he became confused, stumbled several times, and had a brief generalized convulsion that resolved spontaneously.","Upon arrival at the hospital, the patient is lying on the gurney, drooling excessively and muttering incoherently.","His clothes are damp with sweat, and he is visibly trembling.","His breathing is shallow, and he intermittently coughs up small amounts of clear sputum.","The patient\u2019s brother says that no one else on the farm has had similar symptoms today.","He adds that this particular pesticide had a \u201cstrong, bitter\u201d smell, and that the patient accidentally spilled some on his shirt before continuing to work."]},{"sid":25082,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Organophosphate poisoning (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":25083,"type":"psh","lines":["- Tonsillectomy, age 8"]},{"sid":25084,"type":"medications","lines":["He takes no medications"]},{"sid":25085,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":25086,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Father: Hypertension, diagnosed age 65","- Mother: Hypothyroidism","- No family history of neurological disorders or psychiatric illness"]},{"sid":25087,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker.","Alcohol: Occasional (2-3 drinks per month).","Occupation: Crop farmer and agricultural pesticide applicator."]},{"sid":25088,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["Physical examination reveals pinpoint pupils that respond sluggishly to light.","His skin is cool and clammy, and muscle fasciculations are observed in both upper and lower extremities.","Bowel sounds are hyperactive, and there is no abdominal distension or tenderness."]}],"orders":[]}],"problems":[{"did":2900,"code":"T60.0X1A","name":"Organophosphate poisoning","icd_desc":"Toxic effect of organophosphate and carbamate insecticides, accidental (unintentional), initial encounter","snomed":"8260003","snomed_desc":"Organophosphate poisoning","category":"Toxic","acuity":"acute","kind":"active","first_enc":9060,"chapter":19,"block":"T51-T65","docs":[{"enc":9060,"how":"encounter diagnosis"},{"enc":9061,"how":"encounter diagnosis"}],"primary":true},{"did":4031,"code":"J96.02","name":"Acute Hypercapnic Respiratory Failure","icd_desc":"Acute respiratory failure with hypercapnia","snomed":"709110009","snomed_desc":"Acute hypercapnic respiratory failure","category":"Pulmonary","acuity":"acute","kind":"secondary","first_enc":9060,"chapter":10,"block":"J96-J99","docs":[{"enc":9060,"how":"secondary diagnosis"}],"primary":false},{"did":5620,"code":"T65.891A","name":